From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: nivogli <224451320+nivogli@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 17:02:44 +0900
Subject: [PATCH] Convert indirect-count arguments before dynamic rendering
 begins

Each vkCmdDraw[Indexed]IndirectCount ends the Metal render pass to run its
conversion kernel and starts it again, which is expensive on a tile-based
GPU. Before a dynamic rendering instance begins, encode the conversions of
its draws in one compute encoder, so the draws need no restart.

Adopted from https://github.com/nivogli/MoltenVK commit
d9503da35781d19cdf680da1e9883defe4dab0d5.

Modifications: the conversion records the draw count it was sized for, and
the draw uses that count instead of reading the cap again, so a raised cap
cannot make a draw read past the converted buffer. Statistics parameters
and log output are dropped. Hoisting now also stops at vkCmdWaitEvents and
vkCmdExecuteCommands, whose barriers it cannot inspect, and is skipped if
a Metal render encoder is still open.

Classic render passes are not hoisted, as they encode external dependency
barriers as they begin. A multiview pass after the first converts in place,
because the first pass consumes the hoisted conversion. With immediate
encoding the following commands are not recorded yet, so draws also convert
in place.

MVK_PERF_HOIST_INDIRECT_COUNT=0 converts every draw in place.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
